| Term       | Simple Definition                                                 |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Genome     | The complete DNA of an organism.                                  |
| Locus      | The physical location of a gene on a chromosome.                  |
| Exon       | A region retained in mature mRNA after splicing.                  |
| Intron     | A region removed during RNA processing.                           |
| Transcript | An RNA molecule produced from a gene.                             |
| Isoform    | Different versions of RNA or protein produced from the same gene. |
